cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you refer to this software, please cite it as below.
title: Privacyassay
abstract: >-
  A single-file browser fingerprint auditor. It measures what a website can read
  about a visitor's browser and scores how much of that the browser hides,
  weighted by how identifying each reading is. Measurement and scoring both
  happen in the page and no fingerprint is transmitted. The score is the share of
  what this tool checks that a browser hides; it is not an estimate of how rare a
  visitor is, which would require a population of real fingerprints.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Seyed Ehsan
    family-names: Hadi
version: 0.9.1-beta
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/seyedehsanhadi/privacyassay
url: https://privacyassay.com
keywords:
  - browser fingerprinting
  - privacy measurement
  - web privacy
  - anti-fingerprinting
  - storage partitioning
  - web security
